Decode packets where the caller wrote them — PUNKTFUNK LOCAL PATCH.

Not upstream (pyrowave.h carries "TODO: Add support for importing external
memory as GPU buffers"). push_packet copied every packet into payload_data_cpu,
upload_payload copied that again into a staging buffer, and a transfer copied it
into the device-local payload buffer: two CPU copies and one GPU copy of every
AU byte, on top of the client's own reassembly.

pyrowave_decoder_set_payload_memory() takes a buffer the caller owns, mapped and
host-coherent, plus optional R8/R16/R32 linear images aliasing it (the path
mobile GPUs read fastest). pyrowave wraps the handles without owning them, binds
them where it bound its own payload, and stops reallocating it.
pyrowave_decoder_push_packet_in_place() parses a packet that already lies in
that memory and records its word offset in the offset table instead of copying
it. push_packet still copies, into a reserved head of the buffer, so a frame may
mix both. upload_payload now reports failure (a copy overflowing the head), and
decode() returns it.

